  "details": "I think it might be fun to have a props system similar to the avatar system. They would have limited functionality and would be just as useful as a prop on an avatar, but they can be used with any avatar. You could have a sword prop with one character, switch avatars, and then use the same sword with that different avatar. \n\nWhen I am imagining the process to make something like this, i'm imagining a basic armature in unity that you would attach the props to in the same way you would an avatar. You could have previously mentioned sword on the hip and use a physbone like you would on an avatar to be able to grab it and move it around. I do think this would likely require a new SDK, but it would be similar to the avatar SDK so it wouldn't be super hard for makers to get used to.\n\nOther things I can think that could be done with this feature are things like a pet that follows you around (like the amongus astronaut many have already), a gun prop, a really nice crown, a fishing rod that can be cast... These are things that can be found on an avatar easily, but the difference being they can be added to a menu that can be shared like avatars and would scale to the current avatar.",
